#: reports/report_types/aggregate_organisation_report/term_overview.html
msgid ""
"Web servers and domains are examples of digital assets within this "
"framework. Web servers are essential for hosting and serving websites or web "
"applications, while domains represent the online addresses used to access "
"these resources. Other examples of assets in the IT realm include databases, "
"user accounts, software applications, and networking infrastructure. Asset "
"management is a critical aspect of cybersecurity, involving the "
"identification, classification, and protection of these assets to safeguard "
"against threats and ensure the overall security and functionality of an "
"organization's IT environment."
msgstr ""
"Webservers en domeinen binne foarbylden fan digitale assets binnen dit "
"framework. Webservers binne essinsjeel foar it hosten en oanbieden fan "
"websites of webapplikaasjes, wylst domeinen de online adressen binne dy’t "
"brûkt wurde om tagong te krijen ta dizze boarnen. Oare foarbylden fan assets "
"yn it IT-domein binne databases, brûkersaccounts, softwareapplikaasjes en "
"netwurkynfrastruktuer. Assetmanagement is in krúsjaal aspekt fan "
"cybersecurity, dat de identifikaasje, klassifikaasje en beskerming fan dizze "
"assets omfettet om bedrigingen op te kearen en de folsleine feilichheid en "
"funksjonaliteit fan de IT-omjouwing fan in organisaasje te waarboargjen."

#: reports/report_types/aggregate_organisation_report/term_overview.html
msgid ""
"Multiple hostnames that resolve to one IP address where at least one of the "
"hostnames or the IP address has a declared scan level that is at least L1. "
"Type systems are web servers, mail servers and name servers (DNS)."
msgstr ""
"Meardere hostnammen dy’t nei ien IP-adres resolve wêrby op syn minst ien fan "
"de hostnammen mei dat IP-adres in scan-frijwarringsnivo fan op syn minst L1 "
"hat. Type systemen binne webservers, mailservers en nameservers (DNS)."

#: reports/report_types/aggregate_organisation_report/term_overview.html
msgid ""
"A fundamental component of the client-server model. A web server uses "
"protocols like HTTP or HTTPS to facilitate communication between clients and "
"the server."
msgstr ""
"In fûneminteel ûnderdiel fan it client-servermodel. In webserver brûkt "
"protokollen, lykas HTTP of HTTPS om de kommunikaasje te fasilitearjen tusken "
"clients en de server."

#: reports/report_types/aggregate_organisation_report/term_overview.html
msgid ""
"A mail server is a specialized software application or hardware device that "
"facilitates the sending, receiving, and storage of emails within a computer "
"network. Operating on the Simple Mail Transfer Protocol (SMTP) for outgoing "
"messages and either Internet Message Access Protocol (IMAP) or Post Office "
"Protocol (POP) for incoming messages, a mail server manages email "
"communication by routing messages between users and storing them until they "
"are retrieved. The server ensures the efficient and secure transfer of "
"emails, handling tasks such as authentication, spam filtering, and message "
"storage."
msgstr ""
"In mailserver is in spesjalisearre softwareapplikaasje of in "
"hardwareapparaat dat it ferstjoeren, ûntfangen en bewarjen fan e-"
"mailberjochten binnen in kompjûternetwurk fasilitearret. In mailserver, dy’t "
"wurket op basis fan it Simple Mail Tranfer Protokol (SMTP) foar útgeande "
"berjochten en Internet Message Access Protokol (IMAP) of Post Office "
"Protocol (POP) foar ynkommende berjochten, beheart e-mailkommunikaasje troch "
"berjochten tusken brûkers te ferstjoeren en te bewarjen oant se ophelle "
"wurde. De server soarget foar in effisjinte en feilige oerdracht fan e-"
"mailberjochten en fiert taken út lykas autentikaasje, spamfiltering en "
"opslach fan berjochten."

#: reports/report_types/aggregate_organisation_report/term_overview.html
msgid ""
"A nameserver, or Domain Name System (DNS) server, is a critical component of "
"the internet infrastructure responsible for translating human-readable "
"domain names into IP addresses, enabling the seamless navigation of the web. "
"When a user enters a domain name in a web browser, the nameserver is queried "
"to obtain the corresponding IP address of the server hosting the associated "
"website or service."
msgstr ""
"In nameserver, of Domain Name System (DNS)-server, is in kritysk ûnderdiel "
"fan de ynternetinynfrastruktuer dy’t ferantwurdlik is foar it oersetten fan "
"troch minsken lêsbere domeinnammen nei IP-adressen, wêrtroch’t naadleaze "
"navigaasje op it web mooglik is. Wannear’t in brûker in domeinnamme ynfiert "
"yn in webbrowser, dan wurdt de nameserver rieplachte om it byhearrende IP-"
"adres te krijen fan de server dy’t de byhearrende website of service host."

#: reports/report_types/aggregate_organisation_report/term_overview.html
msgid ""
"A DICOM server, which stands for Digital Imaging and Communications in "
"Medicine, is a specialized server designed for the storage, retrieval, and "
"exchange of medical images and related information in the healthcare "
"industry. DICOM is a widely adopted standard that ensures interoperability "
"and consistency in the communication of medical images and associated data "
"among different devices and systems, such as medical imaging equipment, "
"picture archiving and communication systems (PACS), and radiology "
"information systems (RIS). DICOM servers store and manage patient-specific "
"medical images, like X-rays, CT scans, and MRIs, utilizing a standardized "
"format."
msgstr ""
"In DICOM-server, wat stiet foar Digital Imaging and Communications in "
"Medicine, is in spesjalisearre server ûntwurpen foar it bewarjen, opheljen "
"en útwikseljen fan medyske bylden en relatearre ynformaasje yn de "
"sûnenssoarch. DICOM is in breed akseptearre standert dy’t soarget foar "
"ynteroperabiliteit en konsistinsje yn de kommunikaasje fan medyske bylden en "
"byhearrende gegevens tusken ferskillende apparaten en systemen, lykas "
"medyske byldfoarmingsapparatuer, byldargivearrings- en kommunikaasjesystemen "
"(PACS) en radiology-ynformaasjesystemen (RIS). DICOM-servers bewarje "
"pasjintspesifike medyske bylden, lykas röntgenfoto’s, CT-scans en MRI’s en "
"beheare dy mei help fan in standerdisearre formaat."

